cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the method, please cite it as below."
title: "PoT-NZ: Power-of-Two Quantization without Zero"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/FiferitAi/pot-nz"
url: "https://github.com/FiferitAi/pot-nz"
keywords:
  - quantization
  - quantization-aware-training
  - qat
  - power-of-two
  - zero-free quantization
  - model compression
  - language-model
abstract: >-
  PoT-NZ is a quantization-aware training method that uses a uniform grid
  of the form k*n/2^p with the level zero excluded from the grid. The step
  is a power of two, so every representable weight is an exact binary
  fraction, and the grid has exactly 2^(p+1) levels, which makes a code take
  exactly p+1 bits with no dead code and no zero-point. We evaluate the
  method on a small character-level Transformer and on a ~7.3M parameter
  BPE-16k Transformer, compare it against fp32 and int8, and report
  bit-width scaling (p = 2..8), a bit-packing format (SZP1) and a
  zero-mask format (SZM1) for sparse grids.
authors:
  - name: "FiferitAi"
